{"toolCallId":"call_3ee14aac57e6452c8944cb56bdc8c5f3","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md:113:| REQ-007 | With `--quiet`, any warning the script writes to stderr is still written to stderr, so the flag trims stdout only and never silences a diagnostic. |\nspecs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/acceptance-criteria.md:65:| AC-009 | REQ-007 | Given a warning the script writes to stderr, When the script runs with `--quiet`, Then the warning still reaches stderr and stdout holds only the level line | `bash $S --quiet --loc abc 2>&1 >/dev/null` prints `ERROR: --loc must be a positive integer`; `bash $S --quiet --loc 500 --files 15 2>&1 \\| wc -l` prints 1 | Unmet | - |\nspecs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/acceptance-criteria.md:93:is a planning packet. It closes when AC-001 to AC-009 are `Met` with the command\nspecs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md:56:- [ ] T021 Keep every stderr warning on stderr under `--quiet`, implementing REQ-007 (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --quiet --loc abc 2>&1 >/dev/null` prints `ERROR: --loc must be a positive integer`; `bash $S --quiet --loc 500 --files 15 2>&1 | wc -l` prints `1`.\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w27ef8e22cd/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"684dd9","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_40a61c8989194770bbb05cb6076ac18f","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"\nSpec Folder Validation v3.0.0\n\n  Folder: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w27ef8e22cd/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\n  Level:  3\n  Engine: orchestrator\n\n+ FILE_EXISTS: All required files present for Level 3\n! PLACEHOLDER_FILLED: 6 unfilled value token(s) in a Draft packet. Fill each one before the status leaves Draft\n    - implementation-summary.md:50: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Opening hook: 2-3 sentences on what changed and why it matters. Lead with impact.]\n    - implementation-summary.md:61: | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: path] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Created/Modified/Deleted] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What this change accomplishe\n    - implementation-summary.md:70: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: How was this tested, verified and shipped? What was the rollout approach?]\n    - implementation-summary.md:81: | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What was decided] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Active-voice rationale with specific reasoning] |\n    - implementation-summary.md:92: | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Validation, lint, tests, manual check] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: PASS/FAIL with specifics] |\n    - implementation-summary.md:101: 1. **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Limitation]** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Specific detail with workaround if one exists.]\n+ TEMPLATE_SOURCE: Template source headers present\n+ ANCHORS_VALID: Anchors well formed in 5 file(s)\n+ FRONTMATTER_VALID: Frontmatter continuity basics present\n+ FRONTMATTER_MEMORY_BLOCK: All spec-doc frontmatter memory blocks are structurally valid\n+ SPEC_DOC_SUFFICIENCY: All targeted spec-doc anchors meet the sufficiency baseline\n+ MERGE_LEGALITY: No merge plan supplied; legality check skipped\n+ CROSS_ANCHOR_CONTAMINATION: No routing payload supplied; contamination check skipped\n+ POST_SAVE_FINGERPRINT: No post-save payload supplied; fingerprint check skipped\n+ GRAPH_METADATA_PRESENT: Graph metadata checked\nx GENERATED_METADATA_INTEGRITY: Generated metadata integrity found 1 violation(s) (enforced)\n    - graph-metadata.json: SOURCE_FINGERPRINT_MISMATCH: source_fingerprint does not match a re-derive of the current source docs, the stored derived fields may be stale\nx GENERATED_METADATA_DRIFT: Generated metadata drift found 1 drifted field(s) (enforced)\n    - description: stored 'Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh' drifted from fresh 'The level helper has one text output and it is a report, not an answer'\n+ COMMENT_HYGIENE_MARKER: No ephemeral comment-hygiene markers found\n+ SCAFFOLD_NEVER_TOUCHED: Spec status is 'Draft', not Complete; scaffold markers are allowed\n+ STATUS_CROSS_DOC_CONSISTENCY: status cross-doc check not applicable; one status is missing or unclassified\n    - spec.md Status=Draft classified=planned\n    - implementation-summary.md Status=<missing> classified=unknown\n+ AC_COVERAGE: Acceptance coverage gate not active for this level or lifecycle state\n+ TOC_POLICY: TOC policy passed: no TOC headings in non-research spec documents\n+ AI_PROTOCOLS: AI protocols present and complete (4/4)\n+ COMPLEXITY_MATCH: Complexity level consistent with content (Level 3; phases=3, tasks=70, stories=2, scenarios=0)\n+ FOLDER_NAMING: Folder name '001-recommend-level-quiet-flag' follows naming convention\n+ FRONTMATTER_VALUES: Frontmatter values are in the shared list\n+ SOURCE_TAGS: No [SOURCE:] path:line citations in research or review artifacts\n+ GREP_CONVENTION: Grep convention: 5 document(s) conform\n+ LEVEL_MATCH: Level consistent across all files (Level 3)\n+ GRAPH_METADATA_CHILD_DRIFT: children_ids matches the on-disk phase children\n+ GRAPH_METADATA_CHILD_IDENTITY: children_ids entries all carry the packet's own identity\n+ GRAPH_METADATA_SHAPE: graph-metadata.json shape validation passed\n+ METADATA_DISK_PATH_CONSISTENCY: Generated metadata paths match on-disk folder: zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\n+ DESCRIPTION_SHAPE: description.json shape validation passed\n+ NORMALIZER_LINT: No local normalizeScope*/getOptionalString declarations found outside allowed files\n+ SPEC_DOC_INTEGRITY: Spec doc references, metadata, and handover targets resolve cleanly\n+ CANONICAL_SAVE_ROOT_SPEC_REQUIRED: Canonical-save root-spec check not applicable to this folder\n+ CANONICAL_SAVE_SOURCE_DOCS_REQUIRED: Canonical-save source-doc check not applicable to this folder\n+ CANONICAL_SAVE_LINEAGE_REQUIRED: save_lineage is present for the refreshed graph metadata\n+ CANONICAL_SAVE_PACKET_IDENTITY_NORMALIZED: Packet identity is normalized across continuity, description, and graph surfaces\n+ CANONICAL_SAVE_DESCRIPTION_GRAPH_FRESHNESS: Description and graph freshness stay within the canonical-save slack window\n+ CONTINUITY_FRESHNESS: Continuity freshness skipped: SPECKIT_COMPLETION_FRESHNESS is not enabled\n    - code:not_opted_in\n+ LINKS_VALID: All wikilinks under the system-spec-kit skill resolve\n\nSummary: Errors: 2  Warnings: 1\n\nRESULT: FAILED\n\nSome of these are recomputable from the repository:\n  preview  node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/repair-derived.cjs --folder specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\n  apply    add --apply\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w27ef8e22cd/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"b02b36","exit_code":2,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_45a5e85f48394b109160c3928fc49d4f","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"  },\n  \"thresholds\": {\n    \"level_0_max\": ${LEVEL_0_MAX},\n    \"level_1_max\": ${LEVEL_1_MAX},\n    \"level_2_max\": ${LEVEL_2_MAX}\n  }\n}\nEOF\n  fi\n}\n\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# 5. MAIN SCRIPT\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n# Parse command-line arguments\nwhile [[ $# -gt 0 ]]; do\n  case \"$1\" in\n    --loc)\n      if [[ -z \"${2:-}\" ]] || [[ \"$2\" =~ ^-- ]]; then\n        echo \"ERROR: --loc requires a numeric value\" >&2\n        exit 1\n      fi\n      LOC=\"$2\"\n      shift 2\n      ;;\n    --files)\n      if [[ -z \"${2:-}\" ]] || [[ \"$2\" =~ ^-- ]]; then\n        echo \"ERROR: --files requires a numeric value\" >&2\n        exit 1\n      fi\n      FILES=\"$2\"\n      shift 2\n      ;;\n    --auth)\n      HAS_AUTH=true\n      shift\n      ;;\n    --api)\n      HAS_API=true\n      shift\n      ;;\n    --db)\n      HAS_DB=true\n      shift\n      ;;\n    --architectural)\n      HAS_ARCHITECTURAL=true\n      shift\n      ;;\n    --recommend-phases)\n      RECOMMEND_PHASES=true\n      shift\n      ;;\n    --no-recommend-phases)\n      RECOMMEND_PHASES=false\n      shift\n      ;;\n    --phase-threshold)\n      if [[ -z \"${2:-}\" ]] || [[ \"$2\" =~ ^-- ]]; then\n        echo \"ERROR: --phase-threshold requires a numeric value\" >&2\n        exit 1\n      fi\n      PHASE_THRESHOLD=\"$2\"\n      shift 2\n      ;;\n    --json|-j)\n      JSON_OUTPUT=true\n      shift\n      ;;\n    --help|-h)\n      show_help\n      ;;\n    *)\n      echo \"ERROR: Unknown option: $1\" >&2\n      echo \"Use --help for usage information\" >&2\n      exit 1\n      ;;\n  esac\ndone\n\n# Validate numeric inputs first (before numeric comparison)\nif ! [[ \"$LOC\" =~ ^[0-9]+$ ]]; then\n  echo \"ERROR: --loc must be a positive integer\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\n\nif ! [[ \"$FILES\" =~ ^[0-9]+$ ]]; then\n  echo \"ERROR: --files must be a positive integer\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\n\nif ! [[ \"$PHASE_THRESHOLD\" =~ ^[0-9]+$ ]]; then\n  echo \"ERROR: --phase-threshold must be a positive integer\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\n\n# Validate required inputs\nif [[ \"$LOC\" -eq 0 ]] && [[ \"$FILES\" -eq 0 ]]; then\n  echo \"ERROR: At least --loc or --files must be provided\" >&2\n  echo \"Use --help for usage information\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\n\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# 6. CALCULATE SCORES\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nSCORE_LOC=$(calculate_loc_score \"$LOC\")\nSCORE_FILES=$(calculate_files_score \"$FILES\")\nSCORE_RISK=$(calculate_risk_score)\nSCORE_COMPLEXITY=$(calculate_complexity_score)\n\nTOTAL_SCORE=$((SCORE_LOC + SCORE_FILES + SCORE_RISK + SCORE_COMPLEXITY))\n\n# Determine recommended level\ndetermine_level \"$TOTAL_SCORE\"\n\n# Calculate confidence\ncalculate_confidence\n\n# Calculate phase recommendation (default on; opt-out via --no-recommend-phases)\nif [[ \"$RECOMMEND_PHASES\" = true ]]; then\n  determine_phasing\nfi\n\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# 7. OUTPUT RESULTS\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nif [[ \"$JSON_OUTPUT\" = true ]]; then\n  output_json\nelse\n  output_text\nfi\n\nexit 0\n\n# Exit codes:\n#   0 - Success\n#   1 - ERROR: --loc requires a numeric value\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w27ef8e22cd/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"5711ed","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
